# Git hygiene (mandatory)

See [git-workflow.md](../../docs/ecosystem/git-workflow.md).

## Agents must not

- `git push --force`, `git push -f`, or `git push --force-with-lease` **unless** a human explicitly requested history rewrite on **your feature branch only**
- Force-push to update a PR after CI feedback — add commits instead
- Use force push because a prior agent used a bad commit message (amend locally only **before** first push)

## Prefer instead

```bash
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/main
git push origin HEAD
```

## Hooks

`guard-destructive-git.sh` blocks force push (and `reset --hard`, `commit --no-verify`) unless `LI_HOOK_ALLOW=1`.

## If push fails

1. Rebase or merge the base branch — do not force.
2. If you believe force is required, ask the human reviewer; document in PR.
3. Only then: `LI_HOOK_ALLOW=1` + `git push --force-with-lease origin <your-branch>`.

Works with **li-pr-only.mdc** (feature branch + PR only).
